  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian National Police professional ethics hearing involving former police chief Listyo Sigit Prabowo was delayed following his decision to not attend the proceedings. The session was intended to address allegations of unauthorized wiretapping of the President. In response to the absence, police representatives confirmed that the hearing has been moved to November 30, while acknowledging limitations in their ability to compel his attendance. The matter has prompted public and legislative scrutiny, with members of the House of Representatives criticizing the refusal to participate, arguing that such actions may impact the public's trust in the police institution and the core professional standards of the force. Experts from the National Police Commission noted that this is not an unprecedented event for police officers undergoing ethics evaluations, though the high-profile nature of this specific case has generated significant media attention and institutional discussion.",
